hero3NativeAPP — licence status
===============================

NO LICENCE IS GRANTED.

The code written for this project is
Copyright (c) 2026 the repository owner, all rights reserved. No permission to use,
copy, modify or distribute it is given to anyone.

That is the DEFAULT position under copyright law, not a decision — it is written down
here only so the absence of a licence file cannot be mistaken for permission. The
owner may replace this file with a real licence at any time. Until they do, all rights
in that code are reserved.


What this file does NOT cover
-----------------------------
1. `vendor/` — forks of other people's crates, each governed by its own upstream
   licence file. They are NOT relicensed by anything above.

     vendor/wie          MIT                https://github.com/dlunch/wie
     vendor/arm32_cpu    MIT                https://github.com/dlunch/arm32_cpu
     vendor/rustjava     MIT                https://github.com/dlunch/RustJava
     vendor/smaf         MIT                https://github.com/dlunch/smaf
     vendor/smaf_player  MIT                https://github.com/dlunch/smaf
     vendor/softbuffer   MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/rust-windowing/softbuffer
     vendor/oxisynth     LGPL-2.1           https://github.com/PolyMeilex/OxiSynth

   oxisynth is linked statically into `libmain.so`. Anyone who hands an APK built from
   this tree to someone else takes on the LGPL-2.1 obligations for that library.

2. 영웅서기3 — 대지의 성흔 — the game, and everything taken from it. Copyright in the
   game belongs to its rights holders; nothing here covers it and no claim is made to it.
   That includes the packaged game archive (`android_app/app/src/main/assets/hero3_fixed.zip`
   and its pristine copy under `android_app/asset_backup/`, where a checkout carries them —
   they are included only so the app builds), the sound bank built from the game's own
   tones (`wie_android/assets/hero3_ma3.sf3`), the sprite atlas `wie_android/src/icons.bin`,
   the costume sheets under `costumes/` (drawn over the game's own body frames), and the launcher and store art derived from the
   game's title art (`android_app/app/src/main/res/mipmap-*`, `android_app/play/*.png`,
   `android_app/tools/hero3_title_*`).

3. Other third-party assets, each under its own terms:
     wie_web/public/GeneralUser.sf3   GeneralUser GS 2.0.1 by S. Christian Collins; the
                                      licence text is embedded in the file's INFO chunk
     vendor/wie/fonts/neodgm.ttf      NeoDunggeunmo, SIL Open Font License 1.1
                                      (vendor/wie/fonts/OFL.txt)

4. Reverse engineering notes (`tools_re/dis/*`, `MIGRATION_LGT.md` and the other
   design documents) describe that game's binary. They are observations about someone
   else's work.
